Universal Toolkit Project

Project Overview
Universal Toolkit is a modular multi-tool application designed to perform a wide range of computational tasks from a single interface.
The project integrates Math, Number, Arithmetic, Finance, and Conversion toolkits under a centralized main menu system.

The objective is to practice core programming concepts, modular design, and algorithm implementation while building a scalable toolkit-style project.
Features

1) Math Toolkit

Even / Odd Check

Square

Cube

Square Root

GCD / HCF

LCM

Average Calculation

2) Number Toolkit

Prime Number Check

Factorial Calculation

Count Total Divisors

Reverse Number

Sum of Digits

3) Arithmetic Toolkit

Addition

Subtraction

Multiplication

Division

4) Finance Toolkit

Simple Interest

Compound Interest

Percentage Calculation

5) Conversion Toolkit

Temperature Conversion

Celsius → Fahrenheit

Fahrenheit → Celsius

Length Conversion

Meter ↔ Kilometer

Weight Conversion

Kilogram ↔ Gram

Project Structure
UniversalToolkit/
│
├── MainToolkit.java
├── MathToolkit.java
├── NumberToolkit.java
├── ArithmeticToolkit.java
├── FinanceToolkit.java
├── ConversionToolkit.java
└── README.md
Technologies Used



How the Project Works

The MainToolkit class acts as the entry point.

A main menu is displayed to the user.

Based on user selection, the corresponding toolkit module is executed.

Each toolkit is implemented in a separate Java class to maintain modularity and clean structure.


                         
                         How to Run the Project
Step 1: Clone or Download
git clone https://github.com/your-username/UniversalToolkit.git
Step 2: Compile All Files
javac *.java
Step 3: Run Main Program
java MainToolkit
       
